.TH zman "" "Command"
.SH NAME
zman \- GUI manual-page browser
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBzman [\fIoptions\fB]\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.HS
zman -- GUI manual-page browser
Usage:	zman [ options ]
Keys:	^P/^N select page, ^Z/^V page text, ^U clear field
	type a name and press Return to find a page
.HE
.B zman
is the manual browser of the
.SM COHERENT
GUI.
It must be run under the
.B zview
desktop.
It lists every pre-formatted manual page installed under
.B /usr/man
in a multi-column catalog, and shows the selected page \- with bold
and underlining \- in the pane below.
.B zman
takes no page argument on the command line; it accepts the standard
window
.I options
of GUI applications; see
.BR zview .
.PP
The find field in the top bar always has the keyboard focus:
printable characters are appended to it, and RETURN (or the
.B Find
button) jumps to the named page \- by exact name first, then to the
first page of which the typed text is a prefix.
Matching is case-sensitive.
The remaining keys:
.DS
.ta 6n 20n
	\fB^P, ^N\fR	select the previous / next page
	\fB^Z, ^B\fR	page the text up
	\fB^V, ^F\fR	page the text down
	\fBBS, DEL\fR	erase the last character of the find field
	\fB^U\fR	clear the find field
.DE
Because every printable character goes to the find field, SPACE
types a space rather than paging.
.PP
With the mouse, a single click in the catalog loads the page under
the pointer; the two scrollbars on the left edge scroll the catalog
and the text.
A left drag in the text pane selects text and publishes it as the
PRIMARY selection on release, for pasting into other windows with a
middle click.
.SH FILES
.DS
.ta 8n 32n
	/usr/man/*man/*	pre-formatted manual pages
	/usr/hr/icons/man.icn	desktop icon
.DE
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR zview ,
.BR man ,
.B help
.SH NOTES
The catalog is scanned once at start-up; pages installed later do
not appear until
.B zman
is restarted.
It holds at most 250 pages from at most 8 section directories
(those named
.BR *man ).
A page shows at most 600 lines of 200 columns, and the find field
holds 14 characters.
.B zman
only reads the pre-formatted pages; it never runs
.BR nroff .
